ining Employee Training Links EPAF Resources Return Home Have Questions? Human Resources human.resources@msutexas.edu (940) 397-4221 (940) 397-4780 Position Residence Hall Maintenance Foreperson Department Facilities Services Starting Date ASAP Salary $3340 Monthly Plus Benefits Job # S088-26 Budget Position # MH1099 Posted 06/30/2026 Description Performs, supervises, and coordinates general repair and maintenance work for the Office of Housing in the University's residence halls and apartments. Work involves responsibility for planning and completing general carpentry, painting, limited plumbing, limited appliance repairs, limited electrical repairs, and limited air conditioning work. Coordinates larger repairs requiring specific trade skills, in collaboration with Facilities Services personnel and facility remodeling contractors. Orders supplies and materials, establishes and monitors a preventive maintenance schedule. Supervises maintenance staff. Responsible for the overall appearance and repair of the university residence halls and apartments.  Works with Central Plant in scheduling annual inspections and P.M.’s for boilers, elevators, fire sprinklers and fire panels.  Reports to the Manager, Custodial & Residence Life Maintenance. Examples Supervises the planning, assigning and completion of work orders by maintenance staff.  Hires, trains and assigns student helpers to maintenance personnel.  Performs maintenance repairs in residence hall rooms and apartments and orders supplies for the repairs. Services HVAC units in residence halls/apartments. Monitors the completion of all maintenance repairs in a timely fashion. May be asked to move heavy equipment/furniture. Performs minor construction, painting, and limited plumbing, electrical and appliance repairs. Replaces door grills, repairs room and lounge furniture. NOTE: These examples are not inclusive of all work performed, but are a representative sample. Performs other duties as assigned. Physical Condition Some heavy lifting (50 pounds or more) and the ability to work from ladders and in close spaces. Must have sufficient strength and stamina to perform a variety of manual tasks associated with duties. Experience A minimum of 5 years of experience in a broad range of maintenance duties, including mechanical, plumbing, electrical, A/C and heat, carpentry and painting, establishment of preventative maintenance schedules, as well as general maintenance work. Experience in other areas of repair work is desirable. Experience in supervising and/or working in a team environment is required. Knowledge Knowledge of building maintenance methods, including modern methods of use and care of equipment and cleaning supplies. Knowledge of the use of hand and power tools. Must be familiar with the use and care of manual and mechanical types of equipment and tools. Must have a general knowledge of building materials and hardware—familiarity with normal safety procedures and Safety Data Sheets.  Knowledge of fire and safety codes. Education High school diploma or equivalent. Additional Requirements Must be able to maintain effective working relationships with co-workers, supervisors, and departments. Ability to unify subordinates into a cohesive work team. Ability to understand and carry out oral and written instructions. Ability to read blueprints for remodeling and repairs. Demonstrated self-motivated work ethic. *Physical exam required. * Must be available some nights and weekends. Must periodically serve on a standby or on-call basis. Standard Requirements Requires the ability to maintain positive working relationships with students, faculty, staff, and the community. Must adhere to University’s core values: People-Centered, Community, Integrity, Visionary, and Connections, per the MSU Texas Values Journey. Personal cell phone usage may be required to complete position duties, including multi-function authentication requirements. Regular reliable attendance is required. This position is designated as security sensitive (Mod) and requires a criminal background check. Position is designated as a Responsible Employee as outlined by Title IX. May serve as Campus Security Authority as outlined by the Clery Act. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, color, national origin, religion, age, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. To Apply: Submit a state of Texas application, cover letter, resume and list of three references to the Human Resources Department: E-mail : human.resources@msutexas.edu Click here to download your State of Texas Application Midwestern State University Human Resources Department 3410 Taft Boulevard Wichita Falls, TX 76308 Phone: 940-397-4221 Fax:940-397-4780 Last Modified: 01/15/2026 ©  2026  Midwestern State University Site Policies State Privacy Policy Texas Veterans Portal Texas Homeland Security State of Texas State Auditor's Office MSU Texas Privacy Notice Fraud and Misconduct Hotline Campus Safety Statewide Search Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Texas CREWS Title IX Reporting Institutional Resumes Open Records Procedures 3410 Taft Blvd. Wichita Falls TX 76308 (940) 397-4000 Campus Map TTU SYSTEM TEXAS TECH UNIVERSITY TTU HEALTH SCIENCES CENTER TTUHSC EL PASO ANGELO STATE UNIVERSITY"
