ining Employee Training Links EPAF Resources Return Home Have Questions? Human Resources human.resources@msutexas.edu (940) 397-4221 (940) 397-4780 Position Web Specialist Department Information Technology Starting Date ASAP Salary $3847.58 Monthly Plus Benefits Job # S091-26 Budget Position # TD1689 Posted 07/29/2026 Description The Web Specialist uses creative and web development expertise to design, develop, modernize, and improve the website combining aesthetic form, brand standards, and practical functionality creating a unified and consistent presence for Midwestern State University. Examples Provides creative direction (both design and editorial) for all online content. Undertakes ongoing user needs assessments including current users and editors, potential users and editors, and key Dean’s Office Stakeholders. Assists in the development and implementation of a comprehensive communications plan for the Midwestern State University website. Web Specialist I assists the project manager for all non-maintenance web enhancement projects. Web Specialist II serves as the project manager for all non-maintenance web enhancement projects. Generates efficiencies in web maintenance through systematizing ownership, generating targeted training, and prioritizing editing assistance. Logs and analyzes usage patterns, ticket requests, and general time utilization trends and brainstorm ways to develop efficiency for web editing team. Keeps current with appropriate and potentially beneficial advances in web software and electronic design. Works towards a consistent look and feel across the entire University such that all pages would be recognized as part of one broader website. Curates resources or leverages existing online resources for delivering targeted training and makes recommendations for how BEST to guide people to solve technical issues. Ensures compliance with Campus Security, ADA standards and accessibility concerns for all users and inform all editors on respective responsibilities. Liaises with technical staff within University System as needed and to ensure consistency and compliance. Creates and maintains content as requested. Ensures all maintenance and ticket requests maintain consistency in look and feel across the entire University, including all campuses. Performs other related duties and participate in special projects as assigned. Physical Condition . Experience Experience with content management systems required. Knowledge Must have knowledge of web accessibility standards and guidelines, an understanding of version control systems (e.g., Git) and knowledge of back-end technologies ( e.g., PHP).  Must be proficient in web development technologies such as HTML, CSS, and JavaScript. Education College/vocational/technical training with a concentration in computer science, graphic design, journalism, English, technical communication or related fields. Bachelor’s degree preferred but not required. Additional Requirements In accordance with Texas Executive Order GA-48 and applicable state or federal law, this position may involve access to, work on, or conducting research involving critical infrastructure as defined by Texas Business & Commerce Code § 117.001(2) (formerly Texas Business & Commerce Code § 113.001(2)). If this position is determined to relate to critical infrastructure, please be advised that it will require periodic reviews and background checks after hiring, which will include but are not limited to, criminal history and other security-related screenings that will continue for the duration of your employment in that position. Employment is contingent upon the successful completion of these checks. Must be able to perform detailed work accurately and to work effectively with others. Must be dependable and have a positive attitude towards the work environment. Requires good verbal and written communication skills as well as keyboarding skills. Strong skills in planning organization, active listening and attention to details; ability to take initiative, multi-task and work cross-functionally. * Must be available some nights and weekends. Must periodically serve on a standby or on-call basis. Standard Requirements Requires the ability to maintain positive working relationships with students, faculty, staff, and the community. Must adhere to University’s core values: People-Centered, Community, Integrity, Visionary, and Connections, per the MSU Texas Values Journey. Personal cell phone usage may be required to complete position duties, including multi-function authentication requirements. Regular reliable attendance is required. This position is designated as security sensitive (Mod) and requires a criminal background check. Position is designated as a Responsible Employee as outlined by Title IX. May serve as Campus Security Authority as outlined by the Clery Act. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, color, national origin, religion, age, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. To Apply: Submit a state of Texas application, cover letter, resume and list of three references to the Human Resources Department: E-mail : human.resources@msutexas.edu Click here to download your State of Texas Application Midwestern State University Human Resources Department 3410 Taft Boulevard Wichita Falls, TX 76308 Phone: 940-397-4221 Fax:940-397-4780 Last Modified: 01/15/2026 ©  2026  Midwestern State University Site Policies State Privacy Policy Texas Veterans Portal Texas Homeland Security State of Texas State Auditor's Office MSU Texas Privacy Notice Fraud and Misconduct Hotline Campus Safety Statewide Search Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Texas CREWS Title IX Reporting Institutional Resumes Open Records Procedures 3410 Taft Blvd. Wichita Falls TX 76308 (940) 397-4000 Campus Map TTU SYSTEM TEXAS TECH UNIVERSITY TTU HEALTH SCIENCES CENTER TTUHSC EL PASO ANGELO STATE UNIVERSITY"
