ining Employee Training Links EPAF Resources Return Home Have Questions? Human Resources human.resources@msutexas.edu (940) 397-4221 (940) 397-4780 Position Assistant to Associate Vice President, Enrollment Management Department Enrollment Management Starting Date ASAP Salary $2798.75 Monthly Plus Benefits Job # S001-27 Budget Position # C1399 Posted 08/11/2026 Description Provides secretarial and administrative support to the Associate Vice President for Enrollment Management, the Office of Admissions, and the Global Education Office. The work primarily involves performing a variety of complex technical, clerical and administrative duties. Works under the general supervision of the Associate Vice President with latitude for initiative and independent judgment. Manages front office operations. Supervises student assistants. Examples Handles routine, special, and confidential correspondence in a timely and professional manner. Screens visitors, schedules appointments, and maintains files, fiscal records, department webpages, and restricted information. Supervises student assistants by assigning work priorities, monitoring performance, and creating work schedules. Develops special administrative analyses, summary reports, budgetary updates, and communication or presentation documents for the Associate Vice President and relevant Directors within the Division. Performs specialized tasks requiring a high level of skill in typing, English usage, and computer operations. Assists with department program or event planning and implementation. Performs other duties as assigned by the Associate Vice President. Physical Condition Experience Must have extensive experience in general office practices and procedures, including some budgeting and personnel management, and creating a customer centric environment. Experience in scheduling meetings or events, program planning, preparation of professional documents, requisitions, presentations, and reports. Advanced PC experience is required, in Microsoft Office applications. Experience creating and maintaining webpages is preferred. Experience in college student activities, advising, counseling or case management or related administrative or managerial responsibilities is preferred. Knowledge Excellent working knowledge of business English, spelling, and punctuation. Thorough knowledge of office practices, procedures, and equipment. Skill in word processing and advanced computing, including generally accepted Microsoft software applications (e.g. Word, Excel, Powerpoint, and Outlook) as well as technical knowledge of or ability to quickly learn new computer software. Ability to work independently on difficult or complex assignments and to interpret and follow pertinent policies and procedures clearly and accurately. Education Bachelor's degree. Master's degree preferred. E quivalent combination of education and experience sufficient to successfully perform the essential functions of the job acceptable. Additional Requirements Must have excellent verbal and written communication skills, and possess excellent time management, organizational and record-keeping skills, with the ability to work under pressure and uneven time constraints. Must be able to multi-task, work independently, solve complex and technical problems, and exercise sound judgement in difficult situations. Must be able to deliver outstanding, ongoing customer service, and maintain effective working relationships with students, faculty, staff, and the general public. Standard Requirements Requires the ability to maintain positive working relationships with students, faculty, staff, and the community. Must adhere to University’s core values: People-Centered, Community, Integrity, Visionary, and Connections, per the MSU Texas Values Journey. Personal cell phone usage may be required to complete position duties, including multi-function authentication requirements. Regular reliable attendance is required. This position is designated as security sensitive (Mod) and requires a criminal background check. Position is designated as a Responsible Employee as outlined by Title IX. May serve as Campus Security Authority as outlined by the Clery Act. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, color, national origin, religion, age, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. To Apply: Submit a state of Texas application, cover letter, resume and list of three references to the Human Resources Department: E-mail : human.resources@msutexas.edu Click here to download your State of Texas Application Midwestern State University Human Resources Department 3410 Taft Boulevard Wichita Falls, TX 76308 Phone: 940-397-4221 Fax:940-397-4780 Last Modified: 01/15/2026 ©  2026  Midwestern State University Site Policies State Privacy Policy Texas Veterans Portal Texas Homeland Security State of Texas State Auditor's Office MSU Texas Privacy Notice Fraud and Misconduct Hotline Campus Safety Statewide Search Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Texas CREWS Title IX Reporting Institutional Resumes Open Records Procedures 3410 Taft Blvd. Wichita Falls TX 76308 (940) 397-4000 Campus Map TTU SYSTEM TEXAS TECH UNIVERSITY TTU HEALTH SCIENCES CENTER TTUHSC EL PASO ANGELO STATE UNIVERSITY"
