      "description": "Job Posting Details Skip to main content MIDWESTERN STATE UNIVERSITY Apply Visit Give Menu SPIRIT ALWAYS BOLD! Inquire Visit Apply Menu Close panel About Academics Academics Homepage Academic Calendar University Catalogs Majors and Minors Registrar Redwine Honors Program Research Study Abroad Admissions & Aid Undergraduate Graduate International Students Financial Aid Tuition & Costs Scholarships Military Online Popular Links Employment Opportunities Moffett Library MSU Texas Bookstore Student Business Services University Directory Student Life Student Life Homepage Get Involved Health, Wellness & Safety Residence Life & Housing Athletics Login myMSUTexas D2L Faculty & Staff Email Information for Commencement Transcripts Registration, Grades, Etc. Tuition & Fees Calculator Alumni Giving Visit Request Info Home Human Resources Jobs Job Posting Details Related Links Forms Banner 9 - Employee Self Serve Banner 9 - EPAFs Applicant Faculty & Staff Annual Notices Clery Notice and Campus Security Drug-Free Schools and Communities Act Drug and Alcohol Abuse Prevention Program (DAAPP) Employee Clearance Procedures Employee Self Service Faculty and Staff Resources Fraud, Compliance & Ethics Concerns GDPR Privacy Notice House Bill 12 HR Forms HR Newsletter International Visa Sponsorship Guidelines MSU Ready (Emergency Preparedness) Office of Equal Opportunity Operating Policy Manual Public Service Loan Forgiveness (PSLF) Sexual Misconduct Resources & Title IX Staff Holidays TimeClock and Leave Reports Vacation Roll Over Chart Workplace Notices Prospective Employees Campus Map New Faculty and Staff Resources Part Time Employment Student Employment Notice of Filing State Agency Listings Veteran's Preference Information Health, Retirement & Wellness Benefits Insurance - Medical & Dental Retirement Benefits Overview Wellness Resources Managers Employee Clearance Procedures EPAF Resources Manager's Tool Kit Performance Reviews Compensation Job Descriptions Training Employee Training Links EPAF Resources Return Home Have Questions? Human Resources human.resources@msutexas.edu (940) 397-4221 (940) 397-4780 Position International Recruitment and Retention Specialist Department Global Education Office Starting Date ASAP Salary $3224 Monthly Plus Benefits Job # S009-27 Budget Position # CN0892 Posted 08/18/2026 Description Works directly with and reports to Senior Associate Director of Global Education. Works in all areas pertaining to international student recruitment and retention. This includes oversight of the international student application process from prospective student to accepted student. After admission, must work with students through issuance of I-20, and arrival on campus. Once on campus, advises, counsels, and supports international students throughout their educational journey. Must collaborate and work with various campus offices on fulfilling the international student recruitment needs. This position will also serve as a university Designated School Official, assisting with immigration matters related to international students. Examples Must be willing and able to travel internationally, make presentations to interested students, and build partnerships with international institutions and organizations. Must be able to create marketing and promotional materials that are unique to international student admissions.  Must be able to use software system that tracks international student applications, craft targeted recruitment messages, and send those out during the recruitment cycle. Update parents, guardians, advisors, government officials, and other approved 3rd party representatives to discuss international student progress. Coordinate and advise international student organizations to support international students on campus. Counsels international students to help them overcome cultural differences while studying in the United States. Update website related to international student admissions and support. Build relationships with international recruitment agencies and governments to encourage student applications.  Coordinates departmental social media platforms related to international student recruitment and retention. Physical Condition Able to travel internationally on occasion. Experience Must have extensive knowledge of university processes and working with students. Must be able to work with international students in understanding their goals and advising them of appropriate programs. Must be aware and understanding of different cultural norms and differences, and the impact those norms have on international students studying in the United States. Experience working with, supporting, and advocating for the needs of international student populations. Must have international travel or education experience. Must be flexible in a wide range of administrative duties, office machines and procedures, and working in a multi-dimensional office.. Knowledge Knowledge of international student issues and processes preferred, especially the F-1 visa process. Knowledge of international education models and outcomes is required. Must possess good editing and proofreading skills.  Must be knowledgeable in Excel, Word, Power Point, Google Docs, Adobe Photoshop, InDesign, and Outlook.  Must to be able to create promotional content to include videos, flyers, and brochures. Prefer knowledge of Banner software. Must be able to work autonomously. Knowledge of a language other than English is preferred. Education Bachelor’s degree required, preferably in Business/Management, Mass Communication, Public Relations, Counseling, or closely related field. Additional Requirements Should possess good public relations skills, excellent verbal and written skills, and ability to communicate effectively. Must be well organized and able to maintain effective working relationships with co-workers, supervisors, and departments on campus. Ability to commutate with students, faculty members and others both in a one-on-one setting and in large groups.  Demonstrates a self-motivated work ethic. Position not eligible for visa sponsorship. Standard Requirements Requires the ability to maintain positive working relationships with students, faculty, staff, and the community. Must adhere to University’s core values: People-Centered, Community, Integrity, Visionary, and Connections, per the MSU Texas Values Journey. Personal cell phone usage may be required to complete position duties, including multi-function authentication requirements. Regular reliable attendance is required. This position is designated as security sensitive (Mod) and requires a criminal background check. Position is designated as a Responsible Employee as outlined by Title IX. May serve as Campus Security Authority as outlined by the Clery Act. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, color, national origin, religion, age, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. To Apply: Submit a state of Texas application, cover letter, resume and list of three references to the Human Resources Department: E-mail : human.resources@msutexas.edu Click here to download your State of Texas Application Midwestern State University Human Resources Department 3410 Taft Boulevard Wichita Falls, TX 76308 Phone: 940-397-4221 Fax:940-397-4780 Last Modified: 01/15/2026 ©  2026  Midwestern State University Site Policies State Privacy Policy Texas Veterans Portal Texas Homeland Security State of Texas State Auditor's Office MSU Texas Privacy Notice Fraud and Misconduct Hotline Campus Safety Statewide Search Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Texas CREWS Title IX Reporting Institutional Resumes Open Records Procedures 3410 Taft Blvd. Wichita Falls TX 76308 (940) 397-4000 Campus Map TTU SYSTEM TEXAS TECH UNIVERSITY TTU HEALTH SCIENCES CENTER TTUHSC EL PASO ANGELO STATE UNIVERSITY"
    },
