ining Employee Training Links EPAF Resources Return Home Have Questions? Human Resources human.resources@msutexas.edu (940) 397-4221 (940) 397-4780 Position Part Time Bus Driver  (Non-Benefit Eligible) Department Facilities Services Starting Date As Soon as Possible Hourly Rate $22.00 per hour Job # T001-27 Description Work includes transporting passengers while driving diesel powered 51 passenger Motor Coach (or equivalent) or 22 passenger mini-bus, often requiring out of town, overnight and weekend travel. Drives trips as scheduled by Midwestern State University. Monitors and inspects equipment. Performs necessary cleaning, and driver level maintenance. Maintains pre-trip inspection and service records for the buses. Reports to the Auto Mechanic Superintendent. Performs other related duties as assigned. Position Requirements (skills, experience, licensure, etc.) Requires a current Class B CDL with Passenger Endorsement. Standard Requirements Requires the ability to maintain positive working relationships with students, faculty, staff, and the community. Must adhere to University’s core values: People-Centered, Community, Integrity, Visionary, and Connections, per the MSU Texas Values Journey. Personal cell phone usage may be required to complete position duties, including multi-function authentication requirements. Regular reliable attendance is required. This position is designated as security sensitive (Mod) and requires a criminal background check. Position is designated as a Responsible Employee as outlined by Title IX. May serve as Campus Security Authority as outlined by the Clery Act. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to sex, race, color, national origin, religion, age, disability, protected veteran status, or genetic information. To apply: Submit a state of Texas application and list of three references to the Human Resources Department at the address below Midwestern State University Human Resources Department 3410 Taft Boulevard Wichita Falls, TX 76308 Phone : 940-397-4221 Fax : 940-397-4780 E-mail : human.resources@msutexas.edu Click here to download your State of Texas Application Last Modified: 01/15/2026 ©  2026  Midwestern State University Site Policies State Privacy Policy Texas Veterans Portal Texas Homeland Security State of Texas State Auditor's Office MSU Texas Privacy Notice Fraud and Misconduct Hotline Campus Safety Statewide Search Mental Health Resources Public Course Information Texas CREWS Title IX Reporting Institutional Resumes Open Records Procedures 3410 Taft Blvd. Wichita Falls TX 76308 (940) 397-4000 Campus Map TTU SYSTEM TEXAS TECH UNIVERSITY TTU HEALTH SCIENCES CENTER TTUHSC EL PASO ANGELO STATE UNIVERSITY"
